{"units": [{"id": "apodeiknymi-quote2", "translation": "But I must go first to show the way to the chambers."}, {"id": "apodeiknymi-quote3", "translation": "winds displaying opposing blasts against one another,"}, {"id": "apodeiknymi-word1", "translation": "blowing against"}, {"id": "apodeiknymi-word2", "translation": "displaying"}, {"id": "apodeloö-orth1", "translation": "to show clearly"}, {"id": "apodeloö-def1", "translation": "I show clearly"}, {"id": "apodeloö-quote1", "translation": "and having shown clearly, he holds the rough rocky bird."}, {"id": "apodikein-orth1", "translation": "to throw away"}, {"id": "apodikein-def1", "translation": "to throw away"}, {"id": "apodikein-quote1", "translation": "You threw away, you cut off."}, {"id": "apodyromai-orth1", "translation": "to lament"}, {"id": "apodyromai-def1", "translation": "I lament"}, {"id": "apodyromai-quote1", "translation": "to weep for and lament the fortunes."}, {"id": "apozeugnymai-orth1", "translation": "to depart"}, {"id": "apozeugnymai-def1", "translation": "I depart"}, {"id": "apozeugnymai-quote1", "translation": "just as I departed on foot to this place."}, {"id": "apothaumazo-orth1", "translation": "to marvel at"}, {"id": "apothaumazo-def1", "translation": "I marvel at"}, {"id": "apothaumazo-quote1", "translation": "I would like to hear these words and marvel at them."}, {"id": "apothrauo-orth1", "translation": "to shatter"}, {"id": "apothrauo-def1", "translation": "I shatter"}, {"id": "apothrauo-quote1", "translation": "and shatters all the curved ornaments of the Phoenician ship."}, {"id": "apoikia-orth1", "translation": "colony"}, {"id": "apoikia-def1", "translation": "colony"}, {"id": "apoikia-quote1", "translation": "where indeed it is fated for you and your children, Io, to found the distant colony."}, {"id": "apoikos-orth1", "translation": "settler sent from home"}, {"id": "apoikos-def1", "translation": "settler sent from home"}, {"id": "apoikos-quote1", "translation": "A stranger, a settler from the Scythians, distributes the lots of steel."}, {"id": "apoimozo-orth1", "translation": "to lament"}, {"id": "apoimozo-def1", "translation": "I lament"}, {"id": "apoimozo-quote1", "translation": "no longer from a free neck do they lament the fate of their dearest."}, {"id": "apoimozo-quote2", "translation": "Now I praise myself, now I lament being present."}, {"id": "apoimozo-quote3", "translation": "Lament me, the living, more than the dead."}, {"id": "apoina-orth1", "translation": "penalty"}, {"id": "apoina-def1", "translation": "penalty"}, {"id": "apoina-quote1", "translation": "penalties for the insolence of their proud thoughts."}, {"id": "apoina-quote2", "translation": "penalties for the pollutions."}, {"id": "apoina-quote3", "translation": "Know that you will pay me the penalty for this folly."}, {"id": "apoinon_see-orth1", "translation": "penalty"}, {"id": "apoinon_see-word1", "translation": "without toil"}, {"id": "apokeiro-orth1", "translation": "to cut off"}, {"id": "apokeiro-def1", "translation": "I cut off"}, {"id": "apokeiro-quote1", "translation": "of the men whom the god has now cut off."}, {"id": "apoklazo-orth1", "translation": "to cry out"}, {"id": "apoklazo-def1", "translation": "I cry out"}, {"id": "apoklazo-quote1", "translation": "Such things Calchas cried out with great blessings."}, {"id": "apoklao-orth1", "translation": "to lament"}, {"id": "apoklao-def1", "translation": "I lament"}, {"id": "apoklao-quote1", "translation": "to weep for and lament the fortunes."}, {"id": "apokleo-orth1", "translation": "to shut out"}, {"id": "apokleo-def1", "translation": "I shut out"}, {"id": "apokleo-quote1", "translation": "He drove me out and shut me out of the house."}, {"id": "apokope-orth1", "translation": "cutting off"}, {"id": "apokope-def1", "translation": "cutting off"}, {"id": "apokope-quote1", "translation": "bloody, murderous cutting off of the head."}, {"id": "apokorsoomai-orth1", "translation": "to cut one's hair"}, {"id": "apokorsoomai-def1", "translation": "I cut my hair"}, {"id": "apokorsoomai-quote1", "translation": "ἀποκορσωσαμέναις [having cut their hair]: ἀποκειραμέναις [having shorn themselves]; for κόρσας [the hair] means τρίχας [the hair]. Aeschylus in Hypsipyle (fr. 241)."}, {"id": "apokrypto-orth1", "translation": "to hide"}, {"id": "apokrypto-def1", "translation": "I hide"}, {"id": "apokrypto-note1", "translation": "as Archilochus in Stobaeus, Florilegium 110, 10, 3 said: Ζεὺς ἀποκρύψας φάος ηλίου λάμποντος [Zeus hiding the light of the shining sun]."}, {"id": "apokrypto-quote1", "translation": "or the many-colored night will hide the light,"}, {"id": "apokrypto-quote2", "translation": "Zeus hiding the light of the shining sun."}, {"id": "apokteino-orth1", "translation": "to kill"}, {"id": "apokteino-def1", "translation": "I kill"}, {"id": "apokteino-quote1", "translation": "You prepare the weapons, but for them it is a concern to kill."}, {"id": "apokokyo-orth1", "translation": "to lament"}, {"id": "apokokyo-def1", "translation": "I lament"}, {"id": "apokokyo-quote1", "translation": "to lament the soul."}, {"id": "apolaktizo-orth1", "translation": "to reject"}, {"id": "apolaktizo-def1", "translation": "I reject"}, {"id": "apolaktizo-def2", "translation": "I shake off"}, {"id": "apolaktizo-quote1", "translation": "do not reject the bed of Zeus."}, {"id": "apolaktizo-quote2", "translation": "having shaken off sleep."}, {"id": "apolaktismos-orth1", "translation": "rejection"}, {"id": "apolaktismos-def1", "translation": "rejection"}, {"id": "apolaktismos-quote1", "translation": "the falls of men and the rejections of life."}, {"id": "apoleipo-orth1", "translation": "to leave behind"}, {"id": "apoleipo-def1", "translation": "I leave behind"}, {"id": "apoleipo-quote1", "translation": "they left behind the destructive ones."}, {"id": "apoleipo-quote2", "translation": "the end of the immortals will leave behind on high."}, {"id": "apolemos-orth1", "translation": "not to be fought"}, {"id": "apolemos-def1", "translation": "not to be fought"}, {"id": "apolemos-note1", "translation": "war not to be waged: where for the sake of the meter I wrote ἀπολέμιστος [not to be fought]."}, {"id": "apolemos-quote1", "translation": "the unconquerable, unwarlike, unholy divinity."}, {"id": "apolemos-quote2", "translation": "the unconquerable, untamed, unwarlike reverence of old."}, {"id": "apolemos-quote3", "translation": "this war is no war."}, {"id": "apolemos-word1", "translation": "not to be fought"}, {"id": "apolis-orth1", "translation": "cityless"}, {"id": "apolis-note1", "translation": "a city that is no longer a city."}, {"id": "apolis-quote1", "translation": "with whom you made Troy a cityless city, the city of Ilion."}, {"id": "apollymi-orth1", "translation": "to destroy"}, {"id": "apollymi-def1", "translation": "I destroy"}, {"id": "apollymi-def2", "translation": "I have perished"}, {"id": "apollymi-def3", "translation": "I perish"}, {"id": "apollymi-note1", "translation": "but in the next verse ἀπώλεσε δὴ τόδε [he destroyed this] wrongly for ὤλεσε [he destroyed], which Wellauer restored."}, {"id": "apollymi-note2", "translation": "[but Suppl. 918 τἀπολωλότα [the things that have perished] corrupt from τἄμ' όλωλότα [my things that have perished].]"}, {"id": "apollymi-quote1", "translation": "for he never destroyed men."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote2", "translation": "[he destroyed the breath,]"}, {"id": "apollymi-quote3", "translation": "whom Marathon formerly destroyed of the barbarians."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote4", "translation": "Xerxes led them, Xerxes destroyed them."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote5", "translation": "ships led them, ships destroyed them."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote6", "translation": "what youth of allies he destroyed."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote7", "translation": "for you destroyed not with difficulty the second time."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote8", "translation": "he destroyed a dear man."}]}